## 6. How to interpret this

**Unit classes** (one per reach / set / basin / continent and module):

| class | meaning |
|---|---|
| OK | usable output (or exit 0 for modules without per-unit files) |
| NODATA | exit 0, no output, legitimately nothing to do (no SWOT data, ungauged reach, "decided not to run") |
| EXPLAINED | no output / non-zero exit, but an upstream file is missing (usually no `input/swot/<rid>_SWOT.nc`) |
| STUB | output exists but holds no data (hivdi's empty files, all-fill discharge) |
| PARTIAL | consensus discharge present but `time_str` all no_data |
| FAIL | non-zero exit with all inputs present: a real error for that unit |
| SILENT | exit 0, no output and no "no data" message where one is expected (input: rejected query) |
| LOST | started but never finished (OOM, time limit, node failure) |
| CORRUPT | 0-byte or invalid netCDF output |
| NOT_RUN | no record at all although the module ran (task died early, or was cancelled) |
| MISSING | pre-monitor runs only: no output and no ledger to tell NODATA from FAIL |

"Coverage" = estimated share of eligible units (inputs present) whose output holds data, from a probe sample.
Healthy values vary by module and version (e.g. momma anywhere from 0.43 to 0.88 between pipeline versions; busboi/metroman ~0.55), so judge
coverage against a baseline run rather than absolutely. The gate only aborts on near-zero yield or error storms.

**Benign log noise** (ignored by the signature tables): {% for p in benign %}`{{ p }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.

